  "note": "The ONE declaration of the temp-fixture families (t261029-81). Two consumers read this file and neither keeps a prefix list of its own: the sweeper (integration/tools/sweep_tmp_fixtures.py, which deletes) and the alarm face (server/engine/inspection_lane_watchdog.py, which counts the water level). A family declared here is therefore swept AND counted; there is no second list to add it to, so 'swept but never alarmed' cannot be written down by accident. Add a family by appending one record here - never by editing a tuple in code. Field meaning: prefix = the top-level name prefix the producer mints (this IS the delete gate); kind = what the producer leaves behind (dir | file | dir+file); project = who mints it; reason = why this entry is ours to reclaim; producer = producer file:line or a named producer, empty only where the census recorded no owner (rendered as owner=unknown, never guessed); measured = the sample that put the family on the list; added_by = the ticket or sweep round that declared it. Order is attribution order: the first matching prefix wins, so append, do not reorder.",
